<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand II of Aragon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1452–<a href="/years/1516">1516</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-trastamara">House of Trastámara</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-aragon">Aragon</a> was king of Aragon whose marriage to Isabella of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> united the two crowns. Together they completed the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> in 1492, sponsored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a>'s voyage and expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>, laying the foundations of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-aragon.jpg" alt="Ferdinand II of Aragon" width="313" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Sittow · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Michel_Sittow_004.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Under <b>Ferdinand II</b> the Crown joined Castile in the conquest of Granada, completed in 1492, and Gonzalo Fernández de Córdoba won Naples back from France at Cerignola and the Garigliano in 1503.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Isabella I and <b>Ferdinand II</b> fought the Granada War of 1482–1492 with large armies, siege artillery and an efficient supply system, experience that Gonzalo Fernández de Córdoba carried into the Italian Wars.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crown-of-castile">Crown of Castile · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Isabella I and <b>Ferdinand II</b> exploited a split between Abu al-Hasan, his brother Muhammad al-Zaghal and his son Muhammad XII, known as Boabdil, who rebelled against his father in 1482.</blockquote><a href="/empire/emirate-of-granada">Emirate of Granada · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The marriage of Isabella I of Castile and <b>Ferdinand II of Aragon</b> in 1469 had joined their crowns in the person of the monarch, while each kingdom kept its own laws and institutions.</blockquote><a href="/empire/habsburg-spain">Habsburg Spain · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The marriage of <b>Ferdinand II of Aragon</b> and Isabella I of Castile in 1469 then joined the Crowns of Aragon and Castile under the Catholic Monarchs, the foundation of the Spanish monarchy.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Charles VIII of France entered the city in February 1495 almost unopposed but soon withdrew; Louis XII and <b>Ferdinand II of Aragon</b> agreed in 1500 to partition the kingdom, then fell out, and the Spanish commander Gonzalo Fernández de Córdoba, the 'Great Captain', won the Battle of Cerignola,…</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-naples">Kingdom of Naples · Military</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Palacio de los Sada, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. Died in Casa de Santa María. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=42.5,-1.22&amp;year=1493" aria-label="Palacio de los Sada on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4521 653 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Ferdinand II of Aragon"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4971 923h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4971 923h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=42.5,-1.22&amp;year=1493">What was here in 1493? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
